  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The proposed intervention is to add about 2–5 at.% V to the CoCrFeNi matrix.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding 2–5 at.% V will trigger formation of a continuous protective oxide tribolayer.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::003::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The tribolayer will stabilize friction from approximately 25 °C to 800 °C.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The tribolayer will stabilize wear behavior from approximately 25 °C to 800 °C.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed tribolayer will be continuous and adherent.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::003::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The tribolayer will consist primarily of lubricious vanadium oxide, such as V2O5, together with oxides of Co, Cr, Fe, and Ni.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Vanadium addition promotes localized oxidation during sliding.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::003::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Vanadium oxide is lubricious at room temperature.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The resulting vanadium oxide remains thermally stable at elevated temperatures through the proposed test range.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Accumulated tribo-oxidation can form a glaze layer that provides interfacial protection and solid lubrication at high temperature.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::003::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed oxide glaze will be self-renewing throughout sliding.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The glaze layer will suppress excessive adhesive wear.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::003::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The glaze layer will suppress excessive abrasive wear.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::003::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to unmodified CoCrFeNi, the V-modified alloy will have a lower and more stable coefficient of friction over 25–800 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to unmodified CoCrFeNi, the V-modified alloy will have a consistently lower wear rate over 25–800 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Unmodified CoCrFeNi has elevated low-temperature friction and wear because it lacks a sufficient self-lubricating phase.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Unmodified CoCrFeNi has elevated high-temperature friction and wear because it forms a non-protective tribolayer.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed operating boundary is sliding in ambient oxidizing atmosphere from 25 °C to 800 °C.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A controlled comparison will use unmodified CoCrFeNi and CoCrFeNi containing 3 at.% V under identical sliding conditions.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.design",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
